  "prediction": "Every algebraic step of Jacobson 1995 closes in sympy: (S1) Raychaudhuri with theta(p)=sigma(p)=0 gives theta = -lambda R_kk + O(lambda^2); (S2) dQ = kappa eps^2 T_kk A/2, dA = eps^2 R_kk A/2; (S3) dQ = T eta dA with T = hbar kappa/2pi gives T_kk = (hbar eta/2pi) R_kk with kappa, eps, A cancelling; (S4) a symmetric M_ab with M_kk = 0 for every null k is f g_ab (solution space of dimension exactly 1); (S5) the contracted Bianchi identity div(G_ab + Lambda g_ab) = 0 holds identically on test metric families with arbitrary functions; (S6) conservation fixes f = -R/2 + Lambda; (S7) G_ab + Lambda g_ab = (2pi/hbar eta) T_ab and 8 pi G = 2pi/(hbar eta) gives eta = 1/(4 hbar G); (S8) the SI restoration is unique: eta = k_B c^3/(4 G hbar) = k_B/(4 l_P^2); (S9) EGJ shear: allowing sigma(p) != 0 gives a shear viscosity eta_s = hbar eta/(4 pi) = 1/(16 pi G), eta_s/s = hbar/(4 pi); (S10) Schwarzschild consistency: kappa = c^2/(2 r_s), T_H = hbar kappa/(2 pi c k_B), d(Mc^2) = T_H dS.",
